/*******************************************************************************
 * @file    main.c
 * @brief   5E-HTE firmware entry point (new project - the old main() in
 *          ad9361/src/main.c is reference material only, not built; see
 *          INTEGRATION_NOTES.md).
 *
 *          AD9361 bring-up is written directly here (not delegated to a
 *          separate ad9361_setup.c module) - it mirrors how ADI's own
 *          reference ad9361/src/main.c does it: platform wiring, FIR config
 *          and the ad9361_init() call sequence live in the file that owns
 *          main(). The default_init_param/FIR-config literals below are
 *          copied VERBATIM from that reference (byte-for-byte, script-
 *          diffed against the original) - a proven starting point for this
 *          exact chip. Only the platform wiring (GPIO_OPS/SPI_OPS/
 *          GPIO_PARAM/SPI_PARAM resolved directly to the Xilinx ZynqMP
 *          ops/params, since this board only ever has one platform) and the
 *          surrounding bring-up sequence (no DMA/IIO/debug-console/
 *          FMCOMMS5/MCS - none of that applies here) were trimmed.
 *
 *          TODO(confirm): the 60 Msps TX/RX sampling rate and 45 MHz RF
 *          bandwidth below are ADI's reference defaults, not a number from
 *          your spec - if "2.4GHz direct sampling" implies a specific
 *          required sample rate/bandwidth for this application, change the
 *          two ad9361_set_*_sampling_freq() calls and rf_*_bandwidth_hz
 *          fields below accordingly.
 *
 *          Boot order:
 *            1) Ad9361_Bringup() - bring up the AD9361 (SPI/GPIO wiring,
 *               FIR config, TX LO off, RX gain mode, sampling rate). Must
 *               run FIRST: it owns PSU_SPI_0 (the AD9361 chip select)
 *               before BoardApp_Init() reclaims that same physical SPI
 *               controller for the F1956 attenuators - see board_app.c's
 *               SHARED-SPI-BUS NOTE. A failure here is NOT fatal any more
 *               (2026-10-05): the RF spectrum is disabled, everything else
 *               keeps running and the reason is reported to the app.
 *            0) BoardApp_InitLink() runs before all of this - RS422/PC link
 *               only, so the boot log reaches the app live.
 *            2) BoardApp_Init()  - AC/DC power, F1956 attenuators, optical
 *               delay, ADC7928, RS422/PC link (VIP+kria protocol).
 *            3) BoardApp_PollOnce() in a superloop - services the RS422/PC
 *               link, ADC7928 telemetry and the RF spectrum stream
 *               (stream_framer.c: RX1 DMA capture -> 32-pt FFT -> "WAVE",
 *               plus the cached "RFST" RX-config report).
 ******************************************************************************/
#include <stdio.h>

